<body>
    <h1>BARS: View Appointment Pattern</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.1." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Us=
eCase"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.1. </span>Use Case</h2>
<p>Patients accessing their appointments via the NHS app can view important=
 information about their appointment, supporting them to arrive at their ap=
pointment on time and prepared for the appointment.</p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size: 20.0px;letter-spacing: -0.008em;">Overview</sp=
an></p>
<div style=3D"font-family: 'Segoe UI';line-height: 20.0px;color:#172b4d;">
 <p>This use case supports the retrieval of an existing appointment from th=
e healthcare provider that owns and maintains the appointment record.</p>
 <p>The interaction enables an authorised sender to:</p>
 <ul>
  <li>View an existing appointment.</li>
  <li>Retrieve the latest authoritative version of the appointment.</li>
  <li>Obtain appointment status and scheduling information directly from th=
e provider.</li>
  <li>Support downstream workflows such as viewing, updating, cancelling, r=
escheduling or rebooking appointments.</li>
 </ul>
 <p>The use case follows the BaRS Appointment Management Foundation approac=
h, where appointment information is held by the provider and accessed using=
 the Appointment resource.</p>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.2." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Userresear=
ch"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.2. </span>User research</h2>
<p>This use case is based on Wayfinder user research and research with Seco=
ndary Care Service providers, primarily Acute and Community Health Trusts.<=
/p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.3." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-ScopeOverv=
iew"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.3. </span>Scope Overview</h2>
<div style=3D"letter-spacing: normal;font-family: 'Segoe UI';font-size: 14.=
0px;line-height: 20.0px;color:#172b4d;">
 <p><br></p>
 <p>This use case covers:</p>
 <ul>
  <li>Retrieval of a single Appointment resource from the owning receiver, =
where the receiver is considered to be a Provider operating a TIE or a Supp=
lier operating an EPR.</li>
  <li>Retrieval using a known Appointment identifier.</li>
  <li>Access to the latest version of the Appointment resource held by the =
provider.</li>
 </ul>
 <p>This use case does <strong>not</strong> cover:</p>
 <ul>
  <li>Creation of appointments.</li>
  <li>Cancellation.</li>
  <li>Rescheduling.</li>
  <li>Rebooking.</li>
  <li>Slot discovery.</li>
  <li>Referral creation or management.</li>
 </ul>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.4." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Functional=
scope"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.4. </span>Functional scope</h2>
<p><br></p>
<div style=3D"font-family: 'Segoe UI';line-height: 20.0px;color:#172b4d;">
 <h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.4.1." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Service=
Discovery"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.4.1. </span>Service Discovery</h3>
 <ul>
  <li>The provider service must be identified before the read operation is =
performed.</li>
  <li>The provider endpoint must be registered within BaRS <span class=3D"i=
nline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"a18d34f5-048b-4492-b1bd-22ed62b647c1">ser=
vice discovery</span> infrastructure.</li>
  <li>The sender must determine the appropriate provider endpoint before re=
questing the appointment.</li>
 </ul>
 <p><br></p>
 <div style=3D"line-height: 20.0px;">
  <h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.4.2." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Appoin=
tmentRetrieval"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.4.2. </span>Appointment Retriev=
al</h3>
  <ul>
   <li>The provider is the authoritative source of the Appointment resource=
.</li>
   <li>The sender retrieves the Appointment using: GET/Appointment/{id}</li=
>
   <li>The appointment identifier must identify a single appointment owned =
by the provider.</li>
   <li>The provider returns the most current version of the Appointment res=
ource.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><br></p>
 </div>
</div>
<div style=3D"line-height: 20.0px;">
 <h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.4.3." style=3D"font-family: 'Segoe UI';color:#1=
72b4d;" id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-ClinicalSafety"><span class=3D"nh=
-number">1.4.3. </span>Clinical Safety</h3>
 <ul style=3D"font-family: 'Segoe UI';color:#172b4d;">
  <li>The provider remains responsible for the safe presentation and interp=
retation of appointment information.</li>
  <li>Clinical intent must be preserved throughout the interaction.</li>
  <li>Information returned must not be altered by intermediary systems.</li=
>
 </ul>
 <h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.5." style=3D"font-family: 'Segoe UI';color:#172=
b4d;" id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Requirements"><span class=3D"nh-num=
ber">1.5. </span>Requirements</h2>
 <ul style=3D"color:#172b4d;">
  <li data-uuid=3D"dde40281-5546-491f-9989-7cc9a1ea0a4f">The appointment re=
turned MUST be patient facing and intended to be seen by the patient</li>
  <li data-uuid=3D"f7b5cfc3-92e3-41e8-a5bd-4ac3e2d510d3">All patient facing=
 filters MUST be applied at the receiver / supplier side</li>
  <li data-uuid=3D"d21ffc3e-1af7-4c0c-83a3-05a142d4635a">The request MUST m=
eet the minimum data requirements for an appointment, as set out in the MVP=
 definition</li>
 </ul>
 <p><br></p>
 <div style=3D"font-family: 'Segoe UI';line-height: 20.0px;color:#172b4d;">
  <p>The sender:</p>
  <ul>
   <li>Must identify the provider service before requesting an appointment.=
</li>
   <li>Must be able to retrieve a specific appointment using its identifier=
.</li>
   <li>Must display appointment information accurately.</li>
   <li>Must use the latest version returned by the provider for any subsequ=
ent workflow.</li>
   <li>Must perform a read operation before any appointment modification ac=
tivity.</li>
  </ul>
  <div style=3D"line-height: 20.0px;">
   <p><br></p>
   <p>The provider:</p>
   <ul>
    <li>Must support retrieval of an Appointment resource using its identif=
ier.</li>
    <li>Must return the latest version of the Appointment resource held by =
the service.</li>
    <li>Must expose the appointment through the BaRS API endpoint.</li>
    <li>Must preserve the structure and meaning of appointment information.=
</li>
    <li>Must respond with an appropriate error when the appointment cannot =
be found or accessed.</li>
    <li>Must remain the authoritative source of appointment data.</li>
   </ul>
   <h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.6." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Workflo=
w"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.6. </span>Workflow</h2>
   <ol>
    <li data-uuid=3D"5f8229e0-cfaa-4413-80ce-de392fde2a4d"><span class=3D"i=
nline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"52dcb156-541a-4138-ab55-2561a13c4813">Ser=
vice discovery/resolution</span>
     <ol>
      <li data-uuid=3D"ebee98e6-4f53-4cb4-9551-7be0a4d585a2"><span class=3D=
"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"52dcb156-541a-4138-ab55-2561a13c4813">S=
ender identifies the provider service and endpoint through service discover=
y/EPC</span></li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"69f852a1-bf6d-47ed-ade6-e2b2507fd931"><span class=3D=
"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"52dcb156-541a-4138-ab55-2561a13c4813">S=
ender constructs GET/Appointment/{id} using available endpoints</span></li>
     </ol></li>
    <li>Appointment identification=20
     <ol>
      <li data-uuid=3D"6bdfd257-1ee1-4aa2-a3be-498fd05979ed">Sender perform=
s GET/Appointment/{id}</li>
     </ol></li>
    <li>Appointment response=20
     <ol>
      <li data-uuid=3D"c299acf2-f599-4add-998e-3dcbf1cfa85b">Provider/recei=
ver returns the appointment resource</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"f5f46b05-ba41-49ca-9995-c8611ce2c909">Provider accep=
ts _include <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"90bba998-cc26=
-44a5-b2db-1ca2626e164e">variable</span> and returns a single response with=
 multiple co-located resources</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"d302152d-ed4e-4a55-a03c-88263c7c9ac3"><span class=3D=
"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1ddee37e-8141-4866-9ad4-35baba0a3aed">T=
ypical information includes</span>
       <ol>
        <li data-uuid=3D"ae0e10e0-c729-47e8-a746-600da8a110a4"><span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1ddee37e-8141-4866-9ad4-35baba0a3aed=
">Appointment identifier</span></li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"03f2353e-328b-4997-b922-5ac62166c879"><span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1ddee37e-8141-4866-9ad4-35baba0a3aed=
">Location resource</span></li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"21c21c5f-25c7-4ba7-ac85-dc89e6ddfd3f"><span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1ddee37e-8141-4866-9ad4-35baba0a3aed=
">Practitioner resource</span></li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"2571f5d4-6bd3-4c1f-97d3-d8f7d6248876"><span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1ddee37e-8141-4866-9ad4-35baba0a3aed=
">Participant resource</span></li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"78b6f3b8-92ee-4a38-a946-afa9ba7df80c"><span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1ddee37e-8141-4866-9ad4-35baba0a3aed=
">Other</span></li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"1ac338f8-3c2d-4ee2-91a5-33e8dd64baff">Appointment =
type=20
         <ol>
          <li data-uuid=3D"9b0f186d-bb54-4775-8f20-ed3561a5d1b2">e.g. Outpa=
tient (AMB), Community, etc</li>
         </ol></li>
       </ol></li>
     </ol></li>
    <li>Appointment resource conforms to FHIR R4 UK Core</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"356197a9-73fe-40c8-9bec-420e91cfec98">Consumer process=
ing=20
     <ol>
      <li data-uuid=3D"58cae286-4fc9-4b52-8d99-7114244bc4a3">The sender pre=
sents the appointment information to the user or uses it as the basis for s=
ubsequent appointment management workflows</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"6cf0ec7e-cc9d-426d-b107-f3ca980c5f6f">The sender pro=
cesses and handles any errors resulting from the performance of the GET app=
ointment and provides useful information to the patient</li>
     </ol></li>
   </ol>
   <p><br></p>
   <h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.7." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Informa=
tionflow"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.7. </span>Information flow</h2>
   <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-m=
anual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-thumbnail" d=
raggable=3D"false" height=3D"283" src=3D"52c45870d3f088186c978b52a910335c18=
dce7a413578769b58b6a6f70da1358" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/149=
9072310/image-2026-9-10_13-48-26.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D178=
9044506004&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-re=
source-id=3D"1499203184" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-res=
ource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2026-=
9-10_13-48-26.png" data-base-url=3D"https://nhsd-confluence.digital.nhs.uk"=
 data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-conta=
iner-id=3D"1499072310" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"10" tabind=
ex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"297"></span></p>
   <h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.8." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Accepta=
ncecriteria"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.8. </span>Acceptance criteria</h2>
   <p>The use case is successful when:</p>
   <ul>
    <li data-uuid=3D"3fa6131b-1afd-4280-8b05-ed8bd4ec1b1f">The provider is =
identified successfully.</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"16b6d20b-d614-42be-aaf0-a583fdb8b8b5">The appointment =
identifier resolves to a valid appointment.</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"fc733d8c-a9e8-4485-8a07-ce720ebbda1c">The provider ret=
urns the current Appointment resource.</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"6bb0571e-772d-4797-b98c-dc8c566d1418">The sender recei=
ves and displays the information without loss of meaning or structure.</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"a49ec391-c622-4b74-b3a6-d25410947f15">The retrieved ap=
pointment can be used as the basis for subsequent appointment management ac=
tions where required.</li>
   </ul>
   <p><br></p>
   <h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.9." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Onboard=
ing"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.9. </span>&nbsp;Onboarding</h2>
   <p>It is expected that:</p>
   <ul>
    <li data-uuid=3D"7e4e2a91-21e5-4e2e-8a23-784d3d305465">The Patient Care=
 Aggregator will onboard as a Sender</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"42006a2a-78d9-408b-9ce0-4290bf56d0e5">Providers and Su=
ppliers will onboard as Receivers</li>
    <li data-uuid=3D"dac6f3c6-0eb3-4841-90a5-7bebe945d7c5">A new solutions =
assurance model for this pattern will be defined as a result of this use ca=
se</li>
   </ul>
   <p><br></p>
   <h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.9.1." id=3D"BARS:ViewAppointmentPattern-Refer=
ences"><span class=3D"nh-number">1.9.1. </span>References</h3>
  </div>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Appointments Standard Pattern:&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://simplifier.net/gu=
ide/nhsbookingandreferralstandard/Home/Core/1-5-0/Appointment-StandardPatte=
rn?version=3D1.12.0#gsc.tab=3D0" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">N=
HS Booking and Referral Standard</a></p>
<p>Application 1:&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://simplifier.net/guide/nhsbookingan=
dreferralstandard/Home/Applications/BaRS-Applications/Applications/BaRS-APP=
1?version=3D1.12.0#gsc.tab=3D0" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">NH=
S Booking and Referral Standard</a></p>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
